 ```
 
+By default, only `$` is recognized as a shell prompt. The `prompts` parameter
+lists the prompts to recognize instead; for example, `["$", "%", ">"]` also
+recognizes the prompts of zsh (`%`) and cmd (`>`). A prompt must be followed by
+whitespace, and lines in the same code block may use different prompts.
+
 Rationale: It is easier to copy/paste and less noisy if the dollar signs
 are omitted when they are not needed. See
 <https://cirosantilli.com/markdown-style-guide#dollar-signs-in-shell-code>
